# Plithos routing.
#
# Cloudflare Pages serves every .html file at its extensionless path and
# 308s the .html form to it. That normalisation runs BEFORE this file, so a
# `200` rewrite declared here never takes effect: /saints 200 -> the old
# plithos_saints.html was answered with a 308 to /plithos_saints instead.
# The sitemap advertised /saints, Google followed it, got a redirect, and
# filed the page under "Page with redirect" rather than indexing it.
#
# So the public URL of a page must BE its filename. saints.html is served at
# /saints because it is called saints.html, not because of any rule below.
# Do not add rewrites to paper over a filename; rename the file.
#
# Only genuine redirects belong here: paths that are not real filenames and
# must be sent somewhere that is. Never map /x to anything while x.html
# exists - the alias wins and the real page becomes unreachable, which is how
# /prayers once served the calendar.

# The old names of the Saints and the Library, kept so that every link,
# bookmark and search result made before the rename still arrives. Permanent,
# because they are never coming back.
/plithos_saints        /saints    301
/plithos_saints.html   /saints    301
/plithos_reader        /library   301
/plithos_reader.html   /library   301
/reader                /library   301
/calendar              /          301
